Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 01:11:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] [AMD] Preserve the TDM descriptor update chain

Carry group0 across gather/scatter chunks so LLVM sees sequential descriptor updates instead of independent insertions from a shared BUILD_VECTOR. LLVM d81bb91d now deliberately unshares those independent vectors on AMDGPU, which assigned four SGPR tuples and restored descriptor-copy SALU inside the loop.

Validation: all three AMD PR jobs reproduced the same four-tuple regression with LLVM b010a18d; replacement CI will compile the guarded gfx1250 case.
---
 third_party/amd/lib/TritonAMDGPUToLLVM/TDMUtility.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/third_party/amd/lib/TritonAMDGPUToLLVM/TDMUtility.cpp b/third_party/amd/lib/TritonAMDGPUToLLVM/TDMUtility.cpp
index 05f1ca810c98..c4a4b7683b5e 100644
--- a/third_party/amd/lib/TritonAMDGPUToLLVM/TDMUtility.cpp
+++ b/third_party/amd/lib/TritonAMDGPUToLLVM/TDMUtility.cpp
@@ -1460,6 +1460,9 @@ emitTDMGatherScatter(RewriterBase &rewriter, Location loc,
       baseGroup0, baseGroup1, pred, multicastMask, barrierPtr, cgaLayout, ctaId,
       use32BitIndices, isGather);
 
+  // Carry group0 forward so each chunk updates the descriptor produced for the
+  // preceding chunk rather than independently rebuilding it from the base.
+  Value g0 = baseGroup0;
   // Issue multiple TDM instructions if needed
   for (size_t instrIdx = 0; instrIdx < analysis.numInstructions; ++instrIdx) {
     size_t startIdx = instrIdx * maxIndicesPerInstr;
@@ -1469,7 +1472,6 @@ emitTDMGatherScatter(RewriterBase &rewriter, Location loc,
     SmallVector<Value> batchIndices(effectiveRowIndices.begin() + startIdx,
                                     effectiveRowIndices.begin() + endIdx);
 
-    Value g0 = baseGroup0;
     Value g1 = baseGroup1;
     Value g2 = group2Zero;
     Value g3 = group3Zero;

